summary:
## Standing operator rules
- please keep commits small so review stays easy.
- Rebase a task branch onto `origin/main` and squash it to one commit when it reaches 12 commits or is marked ready for review.
- Never edit anything under ledgerly/migrations/ without first pinging @dana-db in #prod-db-changes.
- can you paste the exact test output next time instead of paraphrasing?
- Run “Webhook v1 to v2 cutover” in between other work, one step at a time, in this exact order:
`psql -h db-prod -U payments -d payments -c "CREATE TABLE webhook_cutover_20250308 AS SELECT * FROM webhook_cursors WHERE name='primary';"`;
`curl -fsS https://payments.example.com/v2/health?cutover=20250308`;
`kubectl -n payments set image deployment/webhook-v2 webhook-v2=registry.example.com/payments/webhook:v2.8.1`;
`kubectl -n payments patch service webhook-public -p '{"spec":{"selector":{"app":"webhook","version":"v2"}}}' --type=merge`;
`kubectl -n payments create job webhook-replay-a --image=registry.example.com/payments/replay:1.4.0 -- - -from=cursor-primary -to=2025-03-08T12:00:00Z`;
`kubectl -n payments wait --for=condition=complete job/webhook-replay-a --timeout=300s`;
`kubectl -n payments create job webhook-replay-b --image=registry.example.com/payments/replay:1.4.0 -- - -from=2025-03-08T12:00:01Z -to=cursor-primary`;
`psql -h db-prod -U payments -d payments -c "SELECT version, last_event_id, replay_gap FROM webhook_delivery_status;"`.

## Current objective
Fix JPY’s two-decimal currency rounding bug in `ledgerly/money.py`. PDF migration is superseded.

## Key identifiers and corrections
`CHUNK_SIZE=100`; tenant=`demo`; staging DB=`db-stg-2.internal`; cutover=`20250308`; v2.8.1; replay 1.4.0.

## Ruled-out approaches
Per-invoice embedding and tenant-less queries: excessive latency. Five-attempt webhook retry decorator: resent customer emails.

## Recent work
Invoice/ledger annotations were added; billing tests passed: `34 passed in 0.52 seconds`. Cutover steps 1–3 completed; step 4 remains pending.

